# ── Not ours to publish ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A read-only reference clone of the upstream project routy was re-engineered from.
/9router/

# ── Development only ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Verification rigs, the engineering journal, and the material routy was
# re-engineered from: the upstream inventory, the module and schema designs, the
# UI/UX working documents, and the golden translator corpus. Users download the
# release artifact, which contains the app; none of this belongs in the published
# tree. All of it stays on disk — this only stops it being published.
/rigs/
/docs/project-log.md
/docs/9router-reference.md
/docs/roadmap.md
/docs/backend-architecture.md
/docs/db-design.md
/docs/provider-page.md
/docs/provider-catalog.md
/docs/ui-ux/
/tests/

# ── Local state ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
*.log
.DS_Store
tests/golden/.tmp-data/

# design-phase screenshots — local reference only
routy-ui/.preview/

# ── Never commit ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Release signing material. The public half is committed (lib/release-pubkey.mjs);
# the private half lives offline, and anyone holding it can sign a release every
# install would accept.
*.key
release-signing*

# ── Build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/routy-core/dist/
/routy-ui/dist/
# release artifacts (tarball, checksums, signature)
/dist/
